  "deviations": [],
  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 selects the `landmark_genes` list while loading (hyperparameter `gene_list`; a missing gene raises); the v2 `ElasticNet` preset selects the same list with `scaledGeneExpression(gene_list=landmark_genes)`. The synthetic gene names are in no shipped list, so both sides get a pre-selected matrix and the selection itself is not compared here.",
    "v2 holds features as float32 end to end (`DenseViewFeaturizer` casts to float32, so the estimator receives a float32 matrix); 1.6.1 computes in float64. Features therefore agree to ~1e-7 relative (class forward), not exactly. Ridge solves in float32 in v2: refitting sklearn Ridge on the same matrix in float32 vs float64 differs by 2.4e-5 absolute (predictions ~7), which is the whole Ridge difference (class train).",
    "1.6.1 builds `sklearn.ElasticNet(alpha, l1_ratio)` with sklearn's solver defaults (max_iter=1000, tol=1e-4, cyclic, random_state unset). The v2 `elasticNet` predictor pins exactly these values (`non_tunable_hyperparameters`), so the effective parameters are equal and the coefficients agree to 6e-8 (class forward) without any override.",
    "The first 1.6.1 hyperparameter set (l1_ratio=0, alpha=1) is `Ridge`; the v2 defaults are the same (alpha=1, l1_ratio=0) and build `Ridge(alpha)` without solver settings, as 1.6.1 does. The `ridge` variant runs the unmodified v2 preset."
  ],
